            <ArticleTitle>How dietary measures can help reduce unhealthy blood cholesterol levels.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>33-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While cholesterol is produced naturally by our bodies, a high blood concentration of certain types of cholesterol is a predisposing factor for coronary heart disease. Some of the reasons for developing unhealthy levels of cholesterol are discussed, together with some dietary strategies to reduce them to acceptable levels.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
